  "findings": [
    "Named-function declaration-start coverage improved from 65.4% in all 12 Phase 2 Sol/high samples to 76.9% for Sol and 84.0% for Astra successful Phase 3 samples. The stricter whole-body comparison uses exactly matched successful case/repeat slots and is stored above.",
    "Across the 11 successful canvas outputs, the direct font reference-count probe passes 2 times, the direct shaping-call probe passes 2 times, and glyph-cache/atlas implementation probes pass 0 times. These probes are specific coverage checks, not exhaustive semantic certification.",
    "Astra covers the active-screen assignment in both successful core-2 outputs; Sol covers it in neither. Neither condition attaches both selected mutex-locking sites directly to the mutex node, although the sites occur elsewhere in every core-2 output.",
    "The earlier discovery-to-submission loss recurs: Sol canvas-2 repeat 2 assembled a 301-range draft, passed a filename rather than JSON to the validator, and submitted a reduced 160-range mapping. Its final output omitted font lifetime and device-ownership evidence found by the children. Offline replay confirms the original 301-range draft passes the structural validator.",
    "Compared with the original v2 results on the 68 identical Core/Renderer canvas nodes, v4 selects substantially more unique source lines, but broad source selection does not establish complete semantic coverage."
